rubrics_metrics.guidance:
Quoted indicators (verbatim as presented):
(a) excessive black market activities and sales, drunkenness and other illegal activities; 
(b) a high absent‑without‑leave rate and an excessive incidence of other disciplinary infractions; 
(c) high automobile accident rate; 
(d) excessive venereal disease rate; 
(e) general lack of smartness in appearance and conscientious observance of military duties; 
(f) a complaining attitude toward constituted military authority and those duties essential to maintain high standards of soldierly efficiency. 
These items are to be used as observable metrics showing loss of respect for American authority, harm to reputation among allies, and loss of individual self‑respect among troops.
